Transposed EXL3 prompt experts for mul1 (4-bit routed experts): enables TensorFold's 3-stage cp.async transposed prompt kernels (exl3_prompt.cuh) for the mul1 codebook and routes all 512 4-bit routed experts across the full 3,072-row chunk in one pass (no split-K fp32 partials, no separate SwiGLU/down-rotate/down-finish launches), while the 6-bit shared expert (512) runs through the grouped path via skip = -(512+2). Knob: TF_EXL3_PROMPT_FAST (default 1; 0 restores 1,024-row grouped_body_mtl). Verified: cold prefill +46-50% (1,235/1,227/1,188 -> 1,804/1,828/1,777 tok/s at 4K/16K/65K), 5/5 greedy token hashes byte-identical to stock, and drafts on == drafts off (greedy & T=0.7).

